(4373038, 627086, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think that maybe the saturation is a bit intense - though I can''t say for sure without seeing the original.  It just feels a bit intense.  It''s very colorful this way but as one commenter remarked, it almost seems unreal because there''s no gradation - just distinct bands of color in the sky.  The composition is good, but just a tad static.  Since I don''t know what''s to the right, my suggestion of maybe having the tree to the left and open up some space on the right may not be do-able.  The way the tree is formed, the location of the moon, and the small circular clump of trees in the distance just seems to beg a bit more open space on the right for balance.</td>', 'I think that maybe the saturation is a bit intense - though I can''t say for sure without seeing the original.  It just feels a bit intense.  It''s very colorful this way but as one commenter remarked, it almost seems unreal because there''s no gradation - just distinct bands of color in the sky.  The composition is good, but just a tad static.  Since I don''t know what''s to the right, my suggestion of maybe having the tree to the left and open up some space on the right may not be do-able.  The way the tree is formed, the location of the moon, and the small circular clump of trees in the distance just seems to beg a bit more open space on the right for balance.', '2008-01-08 05:11:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373046, 626956, 68887, '<td valign="top">thanks everyone for comment.. the timing of the shot was the reason why i choose this one.. the light was great but it was also freezing cold! so every vote is a reward for me :) thanks</td>', 'thanks everyone for comment.. the timing of the shot was the reason why i choose this one.. the light was great but it was also freezing cold! so every vote is a reward for me :) thanks', '2008-01-08 05:20:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373053, 625502, 39850, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Larus:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Chinarosepetal:</b></div><hr/><i>although I wonder how it would look without the foreground fence?  :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It would look boring. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Boring, pf - the Aurora Borealis alone, or even the landscape of Iceland, or the <i>stars</i>, none of those are boring (not for me anyway).  <br/> <br/>I was looking through the comments on this image and found some of the comments amusing on the fence.  I studied this image when I voted long enough to see there was a gate - the track in the snow was a giveaway.  Very nice image.  I gave it a 7, which in hindsight was perhaps a bit conservative.  The image can''t be appreciated fully at this size.  I guess it was mostly the ''darker'' areas (but they''re needed and would not matter ''bigger'') and the frame that held it back for me - both very minor though. <i>edit to add what I was originally going to say: the fence makes this - be a ''different'' image again without it</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-08 05:35:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Larus: Originally posted by Chinarosepetal:although I wonder how it would look without the foreground fence?  :)  It would look boring.   Boring, pf - the Aurora Borealis alone, or even the landscape of Iceland, or the stars, none of those are boring (not for me anyway).   I was looking through the comments on this image and found some of the comments amusing on the fence.  I studied this image when I voted long enough to see there was a gate - the track in the snow was a giveaway.  Very nice image.  I gave it a 7, which in hindsight was perhaps a bit conservative.  The image can''t be appreciated fully at this size.  I guess it was mostly the ''darker'' areas (but they''re needed and would not matter ''bigger'') and the frame that held it back for me - both very minor though. edit to add what I was originally going to say: the fence makes this - be a ''different'' image again without it', '2008-01-08 05:33:14.000000', '2008-01-08 05:35:15.000000', 0),
(4373054, 627640, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BrianR:</b></div><hr/><i> Irene your talent is lifting to another level, I would like to see a car trailer next time, HEE HEE HEE. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL!! I''ll do my best.</td>', 'Originally posted by BrianR: Irene your talent is lifting to another level, I would like to see a car trailer next time, HEE HEE HEE.   LOL!! I''ll do my best.', '2008-01-08 05:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
