(4373121, 620911, 30982, '<td valign="top">I liked this quite well, so I don''t think I''ll be of any help in determining why it scored where it did.  I think it conveys a lovely sense of winter calm and the blue toning suits it perfectly.</td>', 'I liked this quite well, so I don''t think I''ll be of any help in determining why it scored where it did.  I think it conveys a lovely sense of winter calm and the blue toning suits it perfectly.', '2008-01-08 06:58:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373123, 626872, 53147, '<td valign="top">Melethia summed this image up for me nicely. The processing isnt to my tastes in this image. A lighter, softer possibly colorful version may have done you better.</td>', 'Melethia summed this image up for me nicely. The processing isnt to my tastes in this image. A lighter, softer possibly colorful version may have done you better.', '2008-01-08 06:59:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373124, 623929, 30982, '<td valign="top">For a portrait you want the eyes to be very sharp - the most in-focus thing in the shot.  They appear a bit soft here.  Try another sharpening pass and see what happens.  If you edit on an LCD screen, it will probably appear too sharp, but upload and see what it looks like from the website.  You can also try sharpening just the eyes, either by masking or selecting them, or using a sharpening spot tool.  <br/> <br/>As for the messy face, yes, I get that this is what you were after.  But do realize that not all viewers find it "cute" - some find it just messy and icky!  :-)</td>', 'For a portrait you want the eyes to be very sharp - the most in-focus thing in the shot.  They appear a bit soft here.  Try another sharpening pass and see what happens.  If you edit on an LCD screen, it will probably appear too sharp, but upload and see what it looks like from the website.  You can also try sharpening just the eyes, either by masking or selecting them, or using a sharpening spot tool.   As for the messy face, yes, I get that this is what you were after.  But do realize that not all viewers find it "cute" - some find it just messy and icky!  :-)', '2008-01-08 07:01:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373126, 624550, 67258, '<td valign="top">I am being very brave returning to this photo!  I would concur with Bassbone - a good macro, but with a little too bright background.  The composition suits the subject well.</td>', 'I am being very brave returning to this photo!  I would concur with Bassbone - a good macro, but with a little too bright background.  The composition suits the subject well.', '2008-01-08 07:02:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373127, 627999, 30982, '<td valign="top">Shows what I know.  I inferred that Clair was a woman, was no longer with us, and this was her room, the light her presence.  I should read up on my French (which I did study once but that was ever so long ago!)  I do like the light - I quite often find myself shooting stuff like this, too.</td>', 'Shows what I know.  I inferred that Clair was a woman, was no longer with us, and this was her room, the light her presence.  I should read up on my French (which I did study once but that was ever so long ago!)  I do like the light - I quite often find myself shooting stuff like this, too.', '2008-01-08 07:03:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373134, 622905, 67258, '<td valign="top">A pleasing composition and colour tones, and very apt for Christmas!  As you know the slight motion blur has hurt it in the voting - in retrospect you could have afforded to increase the shutter speed at the expense of a shallower dof.  Nonetheless, a picture I would have been glad to have taken.</td>', 'A pleasing composition and colour tones, and very apt for Christmas!  As you know the slight motion blur has hurt it in the voting - in retrospect you could have afforded to increase the shutter speed at the expense of a shallower dof.  Nonetheless, a picture I would have been glad to have taken.', '2008-01-08 07:07:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373135, 625574, 1024, '<td valign="top">Incredible detail.  You must be just loving your new macro lens.</td>', 'Incredible detail.  You must be just loving your new macro lens.', '2008-01-08 07:09:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373137, 624387, 67258, '<td valign="top">No way this came last!  I am astounded - I gave a 5, but was torn between that and a 6.  For me the focus on the collar was spot on, as was the dog level perspective, which gave me as a viewer the feeling that I was another dog!...</td>', 'No way this came last!  I am astounded - I gave a 5, but was torn between that and a 6.  For me the focus on the collar was spot on, as was the dog level perspective, which gave me as a viewer the feeling that I was another dog!...', '2008-01-08 07:12:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373140, 627904, 67258, '<td valign="top">To my eyes the dark processing suits the subject, and emphasises the scale and bleakness of the scene.  The interaction between the adult and child sends out a spark of optimistic hope...</td>', 'To my eyes the dark processing suits the subject, and emphasises the scale and bleakness of the scene.  The interaction between the adult and child sends out a spark of optimistic hope...', '2008-01-08 07:16:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373143, 627757, 69109, '<td valign="top">It should have scored higher IMO. One of my favs for the challenge. This photo speaks to me and that is important. An average of 6 means that nearly half the voters think it doesn''t deserve a 6... Not enough flashy colours perhaps!</td>', 'It should have scored higher IMO. One of my favs for the challenge. This photo speaks to me and that is important. An average of 6 means that nearly half the voters think it doesn''t deserve a 6... Not enough flashy colours perhaps!', '2008-01-08 07:20:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373146, 623531, 1024, '<td valign="top">I gave this photo a 7.  I can see why you loved it, its a cute puppy and a beautiful moment.  I think maybe the voters see this as being a snapshot, but the very reasons most of them voted it low are the exact things I like the most.  (ie. the rustic bowl, the mans feet).<br/> <br/>Actually in the overall scheme of things, this did not do too bad.  I am happy to see where it placed.</td>', 'I gave this photo a 7.  I can see why you loved it, its a cute puppy and a beautiful moment.  I think maybe the voters see this as being a snapshot, but the very reasons most of them voted it low are the exact things I like the most.  (ie. the rustic bowl, the mans feet). Actually in the overall scheme of things, this did not do too bad.  I am happy to see where it placed.', '2008-01-08 07:22:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373149, 626466, 77196, '<td valign="top">Ah! What do the voters know? This is an excellent picture. Lighting on the bird, and detail is superb. Big challenge, with lots of entries, people voting fast, I think this just got overlooked by a lot of voters. Definitely deserved much higher than 4.9.</td>', 'Ah! What do the voters know? This is an excellent picture. Lighting on the bird, and detail is superb. Big challenge, with lots of entries, people voting fast, I think this just got overlooked by a lot of voters. Definitely deserved much higher than 4.9.', '2008-01-08 07:25:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373150, 626872, 1024, '<td valign="top">I rather like this shot.  I read the comments and while I can see the points being made, overall this is a gorgeous shot.  I think it would have scored better if the processing was toned down just a bit.  I also wish I could compare it to the color version.</td>', 'I rather like this shot.  I read the comments and while I can see the points being made, overall this is a gorgeous shot.  I think it would have scored better if the processing was toned down just a bit.  I also wish I could compare it to the color version.', '2008-01-08 07:26:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373151, 627639, 1024, '<td valign="top">I was pleased to see how high this actually placed.  This is one of those kind of voyeuristic shots that I love so much.  Well done!</td>', 'I was pleased to see how high this actually placed.  This is one of those kind of voyeuristic shots that I love so much.  Well done!', '2008-01-08 07:28:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373153, 627821, 1024, '<td valign="top">This is one exceptionally well done environmental portrait.  I absolutely loved this in voting. I bet he would love to have a copy of this photo.</td>', 'This is one exceptionally well done environmental portrait.  I absolutely loved this in voting. I bet he would love to have a copy of this photo.', '2008-01-08 07:30:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373155, 620872, 32786, '<td valign="top">just a observation but that guy haas a tuba in front of him and not a trombone. Isn''t he a tuba player??</td>', 'just a observation but that guy haas a tuba in front of him and not a trombone. Isn''t he a tuba player??', '2008-01-08 07:31:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373158, 627229, 1024, '<td valign="top">Melethia summed this shot up extremely well, and there is not much I can add to what she said.  I personally like blur that is intentionally done, as it was here.  I gave this shot a 9.</td>', 'Melethia summed this shot up extremely well, and there is not much I can add to what she said.  I personally like blur that is intentionally done, as it was here.  I gave this shot a 9.', '2008-01-08 07:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373159, 620311, 23458, '<td valign="top">This is an outstanding shot. <br/> <br/>However, the red bandana comes across as little more than an unnecssary distraction - I recall you doing the same thing with a shot of a boy eating a Mango. Didn''t work then and it doesn''t work now. In both cases the power of an otherwise magnificent shot was significantly diminished by your processing decision. <br/> <br/>This shot is strong enough to stand alone as a standard duo-tone. I''m sure you know that....I think you should have more faith in the DPC voter - I don''t think you needed to resort to a gimmick to get a good score on this one. <br/> <br/>Happy new year! <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'This is an outstanding shot.  However, the red bandana comes across as little more than an unnecssary distraction - I recall you doing the same thing with a shot of a boy eating a Mango. Didn''t work then and it doesn''t work now. In both cases the power of an otherwise magnificent shot was significantly diminished by your processing decision.  This shot is strong enough to stand alone as a standard duo-tone. I''m sure you know that....I think you should have more faith in the DPC voter - I don''t think you needed to resort to a gimmick to get a good score on this one.  Happy new year!    ', '2008-01-08 07:34:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373161, 626327, 62511, '<td valign="top">Great composition, great title, nice all around shot! Congrats on your first ribbon!</td>', 'Great composition, great title, nice all around shot! Congrats on your first ribbon!', '2008-01-08 07:37:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373162, 627974, 30982, '<td valign="top">Quite underrated.  The overhanging limb with all the ivy looks as though it''s there just to protect the innocence of children as they come to run past it.  Really a very gorgeous and delightful photograph.</td>', 'Quite underrated.  The overhanging limb with all the ivy looks as though it''s there just to protect the innocence of children as they come to run past it.  Really a very gorgeous and delightful photograph.', '2008-01-08 07:38:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373166, 623929, 84440, '<td valign="top">Terrific shot. Sorry it didn''t do better. Don''t agree with the sharpness comments.</td>', 'Terrific shot. Sorry it didn''t do better. Don''t agree with the sharpness comments.', '2008-01-08 07:43:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373167, 625118, 30982, '<td valign="top">You said you called it the Pool just because you had to name it, but that pool really is kinda the subject, or at least it comes across that way to me as it is presented here.  I like the vertical composition - for some reason I prefer landscapes in portrait mode.  I kinda like it when I scroll down and cut off part of the sky - it adds a bit more emphasis on the foreground colors and textures, which to me is really subject of the shot.<br/> <br/>And don''t eat your lens cap.  I think you made a good choice with this.  If it speaks to you (and I love it when that happens) it can''t be wrong.</td>', 'You said you called it the Pool just because you had to name it, but that pool really is kinda the subject, or at least it comes across that way to me as it is presented here.  I like the vertical composition - for some reason I prefer landscapes in portrait mode.  I kinda like it when I scroll down and cut off part of the sky - it adds a bit more emphasis on the foreground colors and textures, which to me is really subject of the shot. And don''t eat your lens cap.  I think you made a good choice with this.  If it speaks to you (and I love it when that happens) it can''t be wrong.', '2008-01-08 07:44:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373174, 619543, 46782, '<td valign="top">Nice finish but you deserved a ribbon!</td>', 'Nice finish but you deserved a ribbon!', '2008-01-08 07:49:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373188, 623667, 30982, '<td valign="top">You really pulled a lot from the original!  Great processing to get the tonal range.  You mentioned that you did a lot of selective blurring.  In my opinion (and it''s a matter of taste) you overdid the blurring on the clouds a bit.  It kinda gives the impression of them moving but just not quite, if that makes sense.  But I gotta say that you did a very admirable job, from seeing what you wanted to shoot and knowing where to go to get the shot, to some serious post-processing.  And it''s a PB.  That''s not all bad!  Don''t worry - the 6s will come.  (Then go, and you won''t see one again for ages, but that''s DPC for ya.)  And you DID get a 6 from your commenters.  To me, that''s the sign of a successful free study - if a commenter or two likes it.</td>', 'You really pulled a lot from the original!  Great processing to get the tonal range.  You mentioned that you did a lot of selective blurring.  In my opinion (and it''s a matter of taste) you overdid the blurring on the clouds a bit.  It kinda gives the impression of them moving but just not quite, if that makes sense.  But I gotta say that you did a very admirable job, from seeing what you wanted to shoot and knowing where to go to get the shot, to some serious post-processing.  And it''s a PB.  That''s not all bad!  Don''t worry - the 6s will come.  (Then go, and you won''t see one again for ages, but that''s DPC for ya.)  And you DID get a 6 from your commenters.  To me, that''s the sign of a successful free study - if a commenter or two likes it.', '2008-01-08 07:54:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373190, 626914, 1024, '<td valign="top">Lovely fluid lines in the shape of the flamingo and the reflection.</td>', 'Lovely fluid lines in the shape of the flamingo and the reflection.', '2008-01-08 07:54:33.000000', NULL, 0),
