(4373570, 623531, 67152, '<td valign="top">Deb<br/>I didn''t get around to voting on this one, but I would have given it a 6 or 7.   I quite like the story told by the man''s shoes and the relationship to the dog.  The reason I feel you have a story here is how the man''s left foot is slightly askew as if waiting for his dog to finish having the drink.  The way the lines of the dog''s back and the crack in the street intersect at the dog''s head also drew me in.<br/> <br/>This is a risky shot for a FS but I really quite liked it and I woudl not have changed a thing about the shot.  I think it would be funny to see the purple dog edit sometime....</td>', 'DebI didn''t get around to voting on this one, but I would have given it a 6 or 7.   I quite like the story told by the man''s shoes and the relationship to the dog.  The reason I feel you have a story here is how the man''s left foot is slightly askew as if waiting for his dog to finish having the drink.  The way the lines of the dog''s back and the crack in the street intersect at the dog''s head also drew me in. This is a risky shot for a FS but I really quite liked it and I woudl not have changed a thing about the shot.  I think it would be funny to see the purple dog edit sometime....', '2008-01-08 10:33:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373572, 626969, 24454, '<td valign="top">Auuuugh. ..this is so awesome!  Heartmelting.  And disappointingly underrated in my opinion!  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Auuuugh. ..this is so awesome!  Heartmelting.  And disappointingly underrated in my opinion!   ', '2008-01-08 10:34:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373575, 627639, 67152, '<td valign="top">Terry<br/> <br/>I really like this one - very cool.  The reasons I like it are that I can almost see the man being ''hugged'' by the woman (maybe his mom or some other relative) in the painting.  The starkness of the edit adds a lot of melancholy to the shot.  The thick black border creates the illusion of it being a painting within a painting - a nice touch.  I gave it a 7 during voting and probably should have gone higher.</td>', 'Terry I really like this one - very cool.  The reasons I like it are that I can almost see the man being ''hugged'' by the woman (maybe his mom or some other relative) in the painting.  The starkness of the edit adds a lot of melancholy to the shot.  The thick black border creates the illusion of it being a painting within a painting - a nice touch.  I gave it a 7 during voting and probably should have gone higher.', '2008-01-08 10:37:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373576, 620358, 35994, '<td valign="top">Congrats!! I was pleased to see this on the front page, beautiful image.</td>', 'Congrats!! I was pleased to see this on the front page, beautiful image.', '2008-01-08 10:37:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373577, 626969, 84765, '<td valign="top">Thanks SandyP! I also think it is pretty good, probably the best shot I have ever taken. But I guess I have to accept the vote. Any suggestions that could have made it even better?<br/> <br/>Best regards,<br/>Thomas Jessen</td>', 'Thanks SandyP! I also think it is pretty good, probably the best shot I have ever taken. But I guess I have to accept the vote. Any suggestions that could have made it even better? Best regards,Thomas Jessen', '2008-01-08 10:37:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373578, 623531, 24454, '<td valign="top">I adore this photo.  I can imagine the enjoyment that this fellow and the other puppies brought to people at the camp missing the warmth of home.<br/> <br/>Man. . .I am starting to love more and more -- photos that have more soul than dpc high merit!!!!  But somehow, I''m thinking that''s a good thing!<br/> <br/></td>', 'I adore this photo.  I can imagine the enjoyment that this fellow and the other puppies brought to people at the camp missing the warmth of home. Man. . .I am starting to love more and more -- photos that have more soul than dpc high merit!!!!  But somehow, I''m thinking that''s a good thing! ', '2008-01-08 10:39:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373582, 623929, 11800, '<td valign="top">I''m a messy icky hater type so I''ll comment on this. The thing is most people have seen/raised kids. They have seen them snotty nosed, messy, sick, happy, angelic and all the other kid stuff. They have their own treasure trove of pictures just like this one. So....I guess it''s not a unique picture. I know, it has been said that nothing is unique, but look at winning entries of children and I think you will see the difference between this and those right away. There is something in the others that draws the viewer into the scene. Something that clicks emotionally.<br/>However it is really well taken. As a portrait, I like the lighting and his/her little hand up by the cheek. I like the fill-the-frame crop(well, I''d like a little more room around the baby, especially over on the right of the frame) and the detail in the hair and the color is perfect. You did a good job but I really don''t think messy kids are that cute. Lucky I didn''t vote but this opinion might be carried by other voters.<br/>I''d get rid of whatever that white ring is behind the baby. Direct eye contact might be good too.</td>', 'I''m a messy icky hater type so I''ll comment on this. The thing is most people have seen/raised kids. They have seen them snotty nosed, messy, sick, happy, angelic and all the other kid stuff. They have their own treasure trove of pictures just like this one. So....I guess it''s not a unique picture. I know, it has been said that nothing is unique, but look at winning entries of children and I think you will see the difference between this and those right away. There is something in the others that draws the viewer into the scene. Something that clicks emotionally.However it is really well taken. As a portrait, I like the lighting and his/her little hand up by the cheek. I like the fill-the-frame crop(well, I''d like a little more room around the baby, especially over on the right of the frame) and the detail in the hair and the color is perfect. You did a good job but I really don''t think messy kids are that cute. Lucky I didn''t vote but this opinion might be carried by other voters.I''d get rid of whatever that white ring is behind the baby. Direct eye contact might be good too.', '2008-01-08 10:41:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373583, 627821, 67152, '<td valign="top">Laurie<br/> <br/>A funny thing about this photo.  I almost find it a bit unsettling that he is smiling as if just joking with a buddy, not at all concerned about the fire behind him.  Maybe the fire is under control, or it is just a training mission, but the smile really grabbed my attention.  I think it is a good shot and does tell an interesting story, but I just worry that this guy actually set the fire so he could put it out...<br/> <br/>On the processing side (sorry I could not resist!!!) I see in your description that you purposefully did not sharpen his face - an interesting idea, but not the direction I would have gone.  Your title says "Hot!" clearly describing him (and maybe the fire), but since it is likely about him, I think I would have made him jump off the screen a bit more.</td>', 'Laurie A funny thing about this photo.  I almost find it a bit unsettling that he is smiling as if just joking with a buddy, not at all concerned about the fire behind him.  Maybe the fire is under control, or it is just a training mission, but the smile really grabbed my attention.  I think it is a good shot and does tell an interesting story, but I just worry that this guy actually set the fire so he could put it out... On the processing side (sorry I could not resist!!!) I see in your description that you purposefully did not sharpen his face - an interesting idea, but not the direction I would have gone.  Your title says "Hot!" clearly describing him (and maybe the fire), but since it is likely about him, I think I would have made him jump off the screen a bit more.', '2008-01-08 10:42:17.000000', NULL, 0),
