(4373860, 623247, 57421, '<td valign="top">amazing portrait and colors. the composition with the reflection is so cute. how did I miss in when voting?</td>', 'amazing portrait and colors. the composition with the reflection is so cute. how did I miss in when voting?', '2008-01-08 11:58:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373866, 626327, 42013, '<td valign="top">I love the way the tree was butchered on the right side as it grew, yielding to the demands of the house. "Hank, go fetch your axe and cut off some of that tree, it''s scratching our bedroom window when the wind blows." We never plant a sapling with a full realization of its mature size.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-09 12:24:15.</i></td>', 'I love the way the tree was butchered on the right side as it grew, yielding to the demands of the house. "Hank, go fetch your axe and cut off some of that tree, it''s scratching our bedroom window when the wind blows." We never plant a sapling with a full realization of its mature size.', '2008-01-08 12:00:14.000000', '2008-01-09 12:24:15.000000', 0),
(4373890, 621180, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think the composition is fine, and the fact there are tree branches there is quite natural - doesn''t bother me at all.  It''s kind of a pleasant surprise to find a picnic table in the bridge.  You''ve got good exposure on the bridge itself, but the background seems a lot brighter, in need of a bit more contrast, a bit less light.  Can''t much fix that with the exposure but you can darken the trees behind a bit in post processing.  Give it another pass of sharpening and see if it perks it up a bit.</td>', 'I think the composition is fine, and the fact there are tree branches there is quite natural - doesn''t bother me at all.  It''s kind of a pleasant surprise to find a picnic table in the bridge.  You''ve got good exposure on the bridge itself, but the background seems a lot brighter, in need of a bit more contrast, a bit less light.  Can''t much fix that with the exposure but you can darken the trees behind a bit in post processing.  Give it another pass of sharpening and see if it perks it up a bit.', '2008-01-08 12:09:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373901, 626327, 39427, '<td valign="top">I took a trip cross country and tried many times to find a shot like this.  Very well done, congrats on your 1st ribbon</td>', 'I took a trip cross country and tried many times to find a shot like this.  Very well done, congrats on your 1st ribbon', '2008-01-08 12:15:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373904, 626489, 39427, '<td valign="top">another masterpiece... congrats on another blue too.  Are you working for national geographic yet or what?  Get on that.</td>', 'another masterpiece... congrats on another blue too.  Are you working for national geographic yet or what?  Get on that.', '2008-01-08 12:16:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373920, 624367, 39427, '<td valign="top">this is a great shot jamie, congrats on such a high score in a free-study</td>', 'this is a great shot jamie, congrats on such a high score in a free-study', '2008-01-08 12:21:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373944, 627086, 67152, '<td valign="top">I really like the layers created by the different hues in the sky.  The placement of the tree works pretty well.  I gave this a 6 during voting, primarily due to the significant color noise I see in the sky - as if the blues and cyans are not balanced when you modified them in Hue/Sat.  A bit of smoothing either with a brush or using a noise reduction approach would have likely helped a great deal and bumped that score well over 6.<br/> <br/>Cheers!<br/>Peter</td>', 'I really like the layers created by the different hues in the sky.  The placement of the tree works pretty well.  I gave this a 6 during voting, primarily due to the significant color noise I see in the sky - as if the blues and cyans are not balanced when you modified them in Hue/Sat.  A bit of smoothing either with a brush or using a noise reduction approach would have likely helped a great deal and bumped that score well over 6. Cheers!Peter', '2008-01-08 12:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373947, 624367, 50231, '<td valign="top">Stunning shot and model man, great work!</td>', 'Stunning shot and model man, great work!', '2008-01-08 12:34:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373956, 627086, 51538, '<td valign="top">It''s an iconic image of commercial value.  But you need to get that artifact-ing under control in the sky.  Even at this diminutive size, I can clearly see it and it detracts from the image.  Perhaps try running Noise Ninja on the blue and red channels - experiment and make sure that the procedure does not cause posterizing.</td>', 'It''s an iconic image of commercial value.  But you need to get that artifact-ing under control in the sky.  Even at this diminutive size, I can clearly see it and it detracts from the image.  Perhaps try running Noise Ninja on the blue and red channels - experiment and make sure that the procedure does not cause posterizing.', '2008-01-08 12:39:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373957, 626660, 67152, '<td valign="top">Nice work Shez!  Really good and sharp and I love the tongue!</td>', 'Nice work Shez!  Really good and sharp and I love the tongue!', '2008-01-08 12:39:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373965, 626327, 87278, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> makes me want to live there :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>me too!!<br/>Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: makes me want to live there :)   me too!!Congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-01-08 12:41:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373984, 625361, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really like this just the way it is.  DPC does prefer more contrast, more saturation, but I like it simple and subdued like this - it''s more natural.  Another neat feature is that the sun is so tiny compared to the rest of the scene - don''t know why that strikes me as interesting, but it does.</td>', 'I really like this just the way it is.  DPC does prefer more contrast, more saturation, but I like it simple and subdued like this - it''s more natural.  Another neat feature is that the sun is so tiny compared to the rest of the scene - don''t know why that strikes me as interesting, but it does.', '2008-01-08 12:49:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374021, 626327, 58452, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image.  I wouldn''t beat myself up about the dust spot.  I had to really look to find it.  I bet it probably didn''t affect your score a tenth of a point, if that much.  Anyway you''ve accomplished 5 or more of your goals, all with one image.  Congratulations!</td>', 'Beautiful image.  I wouldn''t beat myself up about the dust spot.  I had to really look to find it.  I bet it probably didn''t affect your score a tenth of a point, if that much.  Anyway you''ve accomplished 5 or more of your goals, all with one image.  Congratulations!', '2008-01-08 12:58:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374022, 626327, 9462, '<td valign="top">Woo! Lots of firsts for you here, first ribbon, first 7 and a new personal best!<br/> <br/>Great job... I never even noticed the dusty spot until now.</td>', 'Woo! Lots of firsts for you here, first ribbon, first 7 and a new personal best! Great job... I never even noticed the dusty spot until now.', '2008-01-08 12:58:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374028, 626006, 67152, '<td valign="top">Jon<br/>Now I feel enlightened.  I did not know what this building was until I read your comments.  <br/> <br/>I like the title and i like how you isolated the beautiful shapes of the pagoda top.  I think the center crop is a bold choice for this shot.  With a bold choice I think a bolder processing style may have been in order.  The whites don''t quite seem bright enough as if it is a bit underexposed - a boost in levels could fix most of this. Also, the crop is really tight on top and I think a slightly taller image would have feld less crowded and a bit less closed.  <br/> <br/>To me, the title is screaming for a more wide open composition.  The sky is marvelous and I think bringing it out more would have been a big boost.</td>', 'JonNow I feel enlightened.  I did not know what this building was until I read your comments.   I like the title and i like how you isolated the beautiful shapes of the pagoda top.  I think the center crop is a bold choice for this shot.  With a bold choice I think a bolder processing style may have been in order.  The whites don''t quite seem bright enough as if it is a bit underexposed - a boost in levels could fix most of this. Also, the crop is really tight on top and I think a slightly taller image would have feld less crowded and a bit less closed.   To me, the title is screaming for a more wide open composition.  The sky is marvelous and I think bringing it out more would have been a big boost.', '2008-01-08 13:00:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374031, 619354, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by twade1:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dr.Confuser:</b></div><hr/><i> I generally don''t prefer listing editing steps as the title. If the photo won''t stand alone, listing heroic editing steps doesn''t raise my opinion of the photo. If it was a good subject, reshoot it without over exposing it. This is a photography contest, not a photoshop heroics contest. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m sorry I just don''t get the point of such a mean spirited comment. I, personally, would appreciate it if you would just not bother to comment on my images in the future! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry, I honestly didn''t mean to offend you. On reviewing my comment, I can see how it could be interpreted as mean spirited; especially the last sentence. That was not my intent. When a person writes, it''s not always possible to tell their "tone of voice." I am a very direct person. And my directness sometimes gets me into trouble as it did in this case. Since voting is anonymous, I won''t know a photo is yours and therefore won''t be able to avoid commenting on your specific challenge entries. But I will try harder to keep my comments more constructive.</td>', 'Originally posted by twade1: Originally posted by Dr.Confuser: I generally don''t prefer listing editing steps as the title. If the photo won''t stand alone, listing heroic editing steps doesn''t raise my opinion of the photo. If it was a good subject, reshoot it without over exposing it. This is a photography contest, not a photoshop heroics contest.   I''m sorry I just don''t get the point of such a mean spirited comment. I, personally, would appreciate it if you would just not bother to comment on my images in the future!   Sorry, I honestly didn''t mean to offend you. On reviewing my comment, I can see how it could be interpreted as mean spirited; especially the last sentence. That was not my intent. When a person writes, it''s not always possible to tell their "tone of voice." I am a very direct person. And my directness sometimes gets me into trouble as it did in this case. Since voting is anonymous, I won''t know a photo is yours and therefore won''t be able to avoid commenting on your specific challenge entries. But I will try harder to keep my comments more constructive.', '2008-01-08 13:00:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374041, 620911, 67152, '<td valign="top"><br/>I really find this a refreshing and wonderful scene.  The blues really work for me, using them as a metaphor for the cold of winter.  I think my favorite part of the photo is how these tall pines almost come across as small blades of grass being blown by some wind.  The only thing that is a bit of a negative is that I feel the image seems a bit unbalanced - the darkness of the trees on the right seem to weigh the image down and pull the image down on that side while the brights/ whites on the left don''t quite hold up the image enough.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I really find this a refreshing and wonderful scene.  The blues really work for me, using them as a metaphor for the cold of winter.  I think my favorite part of the photo is how these tall pines almost come across as small blades of grass being blown by some wind.  The only thing that is a bit of a negative is that I feel the image seems a bit unbalanced - the darkness of the trees on the right seem to weigh the image down and pull the image down on that side while the brights/ whites on the left don''t quite hold up the image enough. ', '2008-01-08 13:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374063, 628012, 9462, '<td valign="top">A 4 from me... while it is very original, the execution is blah. It really makes the viewer go "eh?" which as has been previously stated is not what people want in a FS... they want eye candy.</td>', 'A 4 from me... while it is very original, the execution is blah. It really makes the viewer go "eh?" which as has been previously stated is not what people want in a FS... they want eye candy.', '2008-01-08 13:12:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374080, 623485, 58452, '<td valign="top">I like the color on this one Doc.  I wondered how the sun could be up with stars still showing.  But I figured it was some kind of Washington state magik.<br/>But......<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dr. Achoo:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>I caught the tide low enough that I could scramble out onto a large rock in the water between waves. <br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ahem, I feel the need to buy some Canon stock.  What is this?  Your third 5D and you''re climbing out on rocks surrounded by water?  In the gloaming? Perhaps you should check out some waterproof housings!  LOL</td>', 'I like the color on this one Doc.  I wondered how the sun could be up with stars still showing.  But I figured it was some kind of Washington state magik.But...... Originally posted by Dr. Achoo: I caught the tide low enough that I could scramble out onto a large rock in the water between waves.   Ahem, I feel the need to buy some Canon stock.  What is this?  Your third 5D and you''re climbing out on rocks surrounded by water?  In the gloaming? Perhaps you should check out some waterproof housings!  LOL', '2008-01-08 13:18:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4374081, 626872, 9462, '<td valign="top">A 4 from me... I don''t want to notice the HDR effect and this one screams HDR. I quite like the unprocessed one, a bit of +saturation &amp; curves is all I woulda done with it. Most of the time for me, less is more. I don''t even go into Photoshop much these days, I just use my Nikon Capture Editor and I''m done.</td>', 'A 4 from me... I don''t want to notice the HDR effect and this one screams HDR. I quite like the unprocessed one, a bit of +saturation & curves is all I woulda done with it. Most of the time for me, less is more. I don''t even go into Photoshop much these days, I just use my Nikon Capture Editor and I''m done.', '2008-01-08 13:18:19.000000', NULL, 0),
