(4376413, 623531, 61651, '<td valign="top">Love the detail in the care taken to give the dog bowl its own special box - puppies will knock their bowls about a lot. :)  Dynamic and interesting composition, a really soothing kind of shot.</td>', 'Love the detail in the care taken to give the dog bowl its own special box - puppies will knock their bowls about a lot. :)  Dynamic and interesting composition, a really soothing kind of shot.', '2008-01-09 01:50:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376476, 628000, 24111, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the kind comments!</td>', 'Thank you for all the kind comments!', '2008-01-09 02:10:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376628, 626489, 38884, '<td valign="top">WOW! I love it...very powerful! Great job.</td>', 'WOW! I love it...very powerful! Great job.', '2008-01-09 03:22:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376677, 622603, 77287, '<td valign="top">Hi and thank you so much to you all for voting and your kind comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-09 04:35:03.</i></td>', 'Hi and thank you so much to you all for voting and your kind comments.', '2008-01-09 04:33:04.000000', '2008-01-09 04:35:03.000000', 0),
(4376682, 626877, 31637, '<td valign="top">This could be the best moon shot period. Very nice.</td>', 'This could be the best moon shot period. Very nice.', '2008-01-09 04:35:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376685, 626489, 57459, '<td valign="top">MANNY!!!! my number 1 portrait photographer!! GReat JOB for winning the blue ribbon. Of course you deserved it!  Is there an online source I can be directed to for future workshops you''re holding in the states Manny??</td>', 'MANNY!!!! my number 1 portrait photographer!! GReat JOB for winning the blue ribbon. Of course you deserved it!  Is there an online source I can be directed to for future workshops you''re holding in the states Manny??', '2008-01-09 04:37:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376697, 624667, 31637, '<td valign="top">Wow what a face, I stared at this and just got lost for a minute. I think for a guy this big, you need to close aperture to about 5.6. His nose is crisper than most of his face.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-09 04:42:29.</i></td>', 'Wow what a face, I stared at this and just got lost for a minute. I think for a guy this big, you need to close aperture to about 5.6. His nose is crisper than most of his face.', '2008-01-09 04:41:25.000000', '2008-01-09 04:42:29.000000', 0),
(4376737, 627333, 60165, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the comments.<br/> <br/>This entry did a lot worse than I thought. Some thought it was taken with a powerful zoom from the ground (?), but it is taken inflight, as traffic is passing above. When two jet aircraft are passing head on (at different levels, preferrably!), it takes about 3 seconds for each mile you are losing in. Add to that the difficulty of focussing through the thick and multilayered windscreen, and it is somewhat a challenge to get it sharp. The sky is very clean blue aloft, so although I tried to adjust color and contrast, it is not far from what it looks like for real. I used to fly Learjets, and have been up to 48000 feet on one occasion. Besides being very clear from here that the Earth is round, the blue in the sky gets darker and darker, as one is almost at the edge of space here (not much more than 10-15% left here of the mass of the Atmosphere).</td>', 'Thank you for all the comments. This entry did a lot worse than I thought. Some thought it was taken with a powerful zoom from the ground (?), but it is taken inflight, as traffic is passing above. When two jet aircraft are passing head on (at different levels, preferrably!), it takes about 3 seconds for each mile you are losing in. Add to that the difficulty of focussing through the thick and multilayered windscreen, and it is somewhat a challenge to get it sharp. The sky is very clean blue aloft, so although I tried to adjust color and contrast, it is not far from what it looks like for real. I used to fly Learjets, and have been up to 48000 feet on one occasion. Besides being very clear from here that the Earth is round, the blue in the sky gets darker and darker, as one is almost at the edge of space here (not much more than 10-15% left here of the mass of the Atmosphere).', '2008-01-09 05:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376818, 626327, 2553, '<td valign="top">Superb image, and one of my favorites.  Had to laugh when I read that you almost wrecked trying to stop to get this shot - I can so-o-o understand that reaction!  Congratulations!</td>', 'Superb image, and one of my favorites.  Had to laugh when I read that you almost wrecked trying to stop to get this shot - I can so-o-o understand that reaction!  Congratulations!', '2008-01-09 07:02:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376850, 624959, 39825, '<td valign="top">hey, congrats!!! wonderful photo. love it.</td>', 'hey, congrats!!! wonderful photo. love it.', '2008-01-09 07:29:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376868, 626489, 33889, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo.  I think the post processing suits the photo well you have acheived the effect you were going for.  Well done.</td>', 'Excellent photo.  I think the post processing suits the photo well you have acheived the effect you were going for.  Well done.', '2008-01-09 07:57:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376923, 623531, 29009, '<td valign="top">Hi Deb,<br/> <br/>Let''s see, with regard to the technicals it''s pretty solid as many others have noted.  Black and white was definitely the way to go here, and you''ve done a good job with the conversion.  As a side note, my favorite way to add a vignette (in CS2) is to go to Filter/Distort/Lens Correction and then use the vignette sliders moving left to create one instead of correcting one.<br/> <br/>This is definitely one of those shots that needs study to fully appreciate, but at the end of the day it''s a dog drinking from a bowl with a man watching.  There needs to be some interaction somewhere, either with the subjects in the frame (dog actually drinking water, man petting the dog, etc.) or with the subject and the viewer (like if you were more in front of him, but still showing dog lengthwise for depth).  The man''s feet does nothing for me, but I see I''m in the minority there.  I''m not much of a dog person, either, so in the absence of flying water (or milk, or whatever it is) to give me a story or a cute expression on the dog''s face, I''m largely unmoved.  Someone previously mentioned getting down a even bit lower, and I think that might have helped with regard to forcing viewer interaction with the scene and showing them something they don''t ordinarily see.<br/> <br/>It''s a solid shot, and I can definitely see the appeal.  I really think it''s just that I''m not so much of a dog person to have that instant emotional appeal that would make me look deeper to find the hidden treasure in the shot.</td>', 'Hi Deb, Let''s see, with regard to the technicals it''s pretty solid as many others have noted.  Black and white was definitely the way to go here, and you''ve done a good job with the conversion.  As a side note, my favorite way to add a vignette (in CS2) is to go to Filter/Distort/Lens Correction and then use the vignette sliders moving left to create one instead of correcting one. This is definitely one of those shots that needs study to fully appreciate, but at the end of the day it''s a dog drinking from a bowl with a man watching.  There needs to be some interaction somewhere, either with the subjects in the frame (dog actually drinking water, man petting the dog, etc.) or with the subject and the viewer (like if you were more in front of him, but still showing dog lengthwise for depth).  The man''s feet does nothing for me, but I see I''m in the minority there.  I''m not much of a dog person, either, so in the absence of flying water (or milk, or whatever it is) to give me a story or a cute expression on the dog''s face, I''m largely unmoved.  Someone previously mentioned getting down a even bit lower, and I think that might have helped with regard to forcing viewer interaction with the scene and showing them something they don''t ordinarily see. It''s a solid shot, and I can definitely see the appeal.  I really think it''s just that I''m not so much of a dog person to have that instant emotional appeal that would make me look deeper to find the hidden treasure in the shot.', '2008-01-09 08:36:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4376949, 626660, 54778, '<td valign="top">Great processing and love the expression!</td>', 'Great processing and love the expression!', '2008-01-09 08:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377082, 626327, 32997, '<td valign="top">congrats...perfect composition, just a great shot!</td>', 'congrats...perfect composition, just a great shot!', '2008-01-09 09:36:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377188, 623985, 35892, '<td valign="top">i thought it was just a bit too bright<br/></td>', 'i thought it was just a bit too bright', '2008-01-09 10:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377195, 625646, 35892, '<td valign="top">i thought there were too many dark area''s</td>', 'i thought there were too many dark area''s', '2008-01-09 10:20:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377203, 624387, 35892, '<td valign="top">too much out of focus--i would have went with 1 of your outtakes a couple of them are very nice and would have scored better in my mind</td>', 'too much out of focus--i would have went with 1 of your outtakes a couple of them are very nice and would have scored better in my mind', '2008-01-09 10:24:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377279, 627904, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow.  What a story.  Or stories.  Standing on the beach in stormy weather is an awesome experience (in the literal sense of "creates awe"), and you managed to combine that with the emotional oomph of time spent with a parent (or grandparent).  I find the contrast in the first two comments amusing.</td>', 'Wow.  What a story.  Or stories.  Standing on the beach in stormy weather is an awesome experience (in the literal sense of "creates awe"), and you managed to combine that with the emotional oomph of time spent with a parent (or grandparent).  I find the contrast in the first two comments amusing.', '2008-01-09 10:39:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377313, 620981, 67697, '<td valign="top">I liked seeing this one during the challenge.  I thought the moment captured and the processing gave it such an authentic feel.  Plus the soldiers in silhouette in the background is pretty cool!</td>', 'I liked seeing this one during the challenge.  I thought the moment captured and the processing gave it such an authentic feel.  Plus the soldiers in silhouette in the background is pretty cool!', '2008-01-09 10:50:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377353, 627904, 67697, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous, sentimental, and moody.  Love it!</td>', 'Gorgeous, sentimental, and moody.  Love it!', '2008-01-09 11:00:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377415, 620561, 60862, '<td valign="top">*rolls his eyes at the prudes*  This is a wonderful shot, Richard.  I guess some people want to pretend that lions don''t eat other animals, baby mammals all survive, and pregnancies occur because of winks and nudges.</td>', '*rolls his eyes at the prudes*  This is a wonderful shot, Richard.  I guess some people want to pretend that lions don''t eat other animals, baby mammals all survive, and pregnancies occur because of winks and nudges.', '2008-01-09 11:21:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377476, 625638, 70661, '<td valign="top">Rob, This is so beautiful! Many congrats!!</td>', 'Rob, This is so beautiful! Many congrats!!', '2008-01-09 11:40:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377500, 626489, 34412, '<td valign="top">Manny...<br/> <br/>You are a great photographer and a master of the art of photography. I onlt wish I know you personally to teach me the tricks. Congrats on another win!<br/> <br/>As I am from Africa, I hail you as KING OF THE ARTS.</td>', 'Manny... You are a great photographer and a master of the art of photography. I onlt wish I know you personally to teach me the tricks. Congrats on another win! As I am from Africa, I hail you as KING OF THE ARTS.', '2008-01-09 11:47:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377583, 626483, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like the strong lines and the nice framing on the side. Maybe too much white space in the sky, the would be the only minor thing I could suggest. Good work.</td>', 'I like the strong lines and the nice framing on the side. Maybe too much white space in the sky, the would be the only minor thing I could suggest. Good work.', '2008-01-09 12:11:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4377890, 625638, 63398, '<td valign="top">Rob, just lovely! Congrats on a fine offering!</td>', 'Rob, just lovely! Congrats on a fine offering!', '2008-01-09 13:29:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4378037, 624990, 56002, '<td valign="top">A couple of people have asked the location...<br/>This was taken on the East side of Cozumel.<br/> <br/>As was my entry for the hidden city<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=625023" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/791/120/625023.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/791/120/625023.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/791/120/625023.jpg"/></a> <br/>Which is adjacent to Coconuts Bar and Grill<br/>(an excellent place to refresh)</td>', 'A couple of people have asked the location...This was taken on the East side of Cozumel. As was my entry for the hidden city Which is adjacent to Coconuts Bar and Grill(an excellent place to refresh)', '2008-01-09 14:12:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4378066, 626489, 3746, '<td valign="top">Had this pegged as the winner.. well done manny.</td>', 'Had this pegged as the winner.. well done manny.', '2008-01-09 14:22:45.000000', NULL, 0),
