(4428222, 627968, 2764, '<td valign="top">A commenter called this a "candid" but it is a carefully composed and executed photo, almost text book.  The triangle of lights, the leading lines which lead into a spot of light draw the viewer in to look more closely at the image, a lovely balance of black and white, vignetting on the edges to make the scene more intense, the couple, place in the rule of thirds point of interest are out of focus perhaps suggesting the movement of a couple through space and time as they make a life together, the road symbolizing the pathway of like leads to a bright spot of hope. The repeating streetlights reminding  if mini suns saying that day will follow day will follow day, adding a fourth dimension of time to the photo. Theres a LOT more in this photo than a "candid".  Look again voters.<br/> <br/>PS - I don''t enter many challenges, that doesnt make me a troll voter, I don''t take great photos but I DO like to look at great photos.</td>', 'A commenter called this a "candid" but it is a carefully composed and executed photo, almost text book.  The triangle of lights, the leading lines which lead into a spot of light draw the viewer in to look more closely at the image, a lovely balance of black and white, vignetting on the edges to make the scene more intense, the couple, place in the rule of thirds point of interest are out of focus perhaps suggesting the movement of a couple through space and time as they make a life together, the road symbolizing the pathway of like leads to a bright spot of hope. The repeating streetlights reminding  if mini suns saying that day will follow day will follow day, adding a fourth dimension of time to the photo. Theres a LOT more in this photo than a "candid".  Look again voters. PS - I don''t enter many challenges, that doesnt make me a troll voter, I don''t take great photos but I DO like to look at great photos.', '2008-01-27 08:09:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4434443, 627766, 53814, '<td valign="top">Wonderful photo. Unlike most of the voters, my only complaint is that the bird IS recognizable. Without the small tail giving away it''s identity, this sea creature could have scored even lower, but would have been a better piece of art. Don''t compromise your photography for a high DPC score unless you are doing it intentionally.</td>', 'Wonderful photo. Unlike most of the voters, my only complaint is that the bird IS recognizable. Without the small tail giving away it''s identity, this sea creature could have scored even lower, but would have been a better piece of art. Don''t compromise your photography for a high DPC score unless you are doing it intentionally.', '2008-01-28 19:26:52.000000', NULL, 0),
